{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_21e0c175660cab9d8b725ef55a3c38fd3a157f2ff9850e9029692256bc265bcd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"langwatch/scenario@29dea3374ef4 snapshot 38fb07a586afa0be","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0d4ad830975661c2a26768570d4c6b2669b6966866ca032768dd50bd21e6861b"],"source_ids":["src_34db99264cff54e2817a13a0f63b1bcc"],"text":"Voice surface includes scenario.audio() for injecting clips, background_noise effects, scenario.interrupt(), result.audio.save() capture, and result.latency reporting TTFB plus p50/p95.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_55862db130039e88f82b05c442f3be1e8f927add7e5b1481687a7597816a4c68","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"langwatch/scenario@29dea3374ef4 snapshot 38fb07a586afa0be","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_92c8e824e497c14bb1a00c0af6dc8b5f99068bacae6d7b210e2b52781ec20324","slc_a1ca79fe028a6d75de1f179daba4388fcb65db129531df9f056f4fc2a519d28b","slc_b602de7db218d84d0da3f076e7343c54c6e7e2f8f6dab0d650f63236ff152611"],"source_ids":["src_34db99264cff54e2817a13a0f63b1bcc"],"text":"A cache_key option makes the simulated user's input repeatable for a given scenario, and a @scenario.cache decorator caches decorated calls keyed by arguments, scenario, and cache_key.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_64c7a59044579d505e427546a8ccfc05eda760202ef5c28490a7fd71db34c5c4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"langwatch/scenario@29dea3374ef4 snapshot 38fb07a586afa0be","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_30a98d6e81a552ba25f1cbce69d56c03c03618d948adab8ecfde30127b3df138","slc_9875fa4627336e1fee0ebc05f6d817225a8cd4c00b31eaee3e8ebf67cdc7d01d","slc_decc2af664e07e327603a2d9cf8030276a09f31cd6ac2e6f59bd01831465ccce","slc_e4dc610b74bf37cdc2c6fa612bc2708f2b0ca84d7aeb414054fd3759f69600b0"],"source_ids":["src_34db99264cff54e2817a13a0f63b1bcc"],"text":"The core entrypoint is scenario.run(), taking a name, description, agents list, optional script of steps, and optional max_turns; script steps are functions receiving the scenario state.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8ad4adc84db8c80636513c166125c588ab4243bc851216c4450407b3b29bca50","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"langwatch/scenario@29dea3374ef4 snapshot 38fb07a586afa0be","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_73798bf61b9623704d06111a2bb675ad3136643b62b1607bb32ea561c98ddf92"],"source_ids":["src_34db99264cff54e2817a13a0f63b1bcc"],"text":"Audio dependencies such as ffmpeg, webrtcvad and websockets ship as hard dependencies of the Python package, included in a plain pip install with no extras flag.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9ab498d6322a3f7e85de5638ef37882a8135902285b8692f80400301a3459312","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"langwatch/scenario@29dea3374ef4 snapshot 38fb07a586afa0be","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1f5b6f6ad59a02716bff5a83b7cd8ccaf1d65d7b2c42ffaabf55512babbe4a3d"],"source_ids":["src_34db99264cff54e2817a13a0f63b1bcc"],"text":"Agents are integrated by implementing a single call() method, and the framework is documented as available in Python, TypeScript and Go.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c70d919d7bd61b458207f87e2c464837cc45b4884c07431f2f7ea130ec6da592","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"langwatch/scenario@29dea3374ef4 snapshot 38fb07a586afa0be","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_12e19875882eb7f83df2081dd1ec3ef69dd1e30b7a198cdeece42f5a7f367efe","slc_27014c42d849cb49f7ca5244d9affb3a994d8fbf04b5911ba63e0c6ebc55d68c","slc_31c936eca3065ee1a2228c33d6af5dab89c0fceaff774e576b8f9444ff084e9f","slc_d404ab1b43b6ed6720baf92d1a77368ae640178d61f904727efa46a538862740"],"source_ids":["src_145e81dac7af546485786655633054d8"],"text":"A proposed ADR moves voice STT/TTS provider state from module-global singletons to per-run ScenarioConfig.voice, because global provider state is unsafe under concurrent runs; Python still carries the global-state design.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cf6ae7c67e0e99424a020fbea9b3910acfab18c2fe87cfd4a8d08bde248cfd36","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"langwatch/scenario@29dea3374ef4 snapshot 38fb07a586afa0be","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5d0b4babbacfef5424b5ff1de725fe6f9e041924a4842955e837e35a4decec5f"],"source_ids":["src_34db99264cff54e2817a13a0f63b1bcc"],"text":"The judge and user simulator rely on LLMs, so even an ElevenLabs-only voice test requires an OPENAI_API_KEY unless both are swapped via scenario.configure.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_daf4e583f416bb6e19a3f09b11cbfaacf117b27af3d458bfa9457b9dab85b892","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"langwatch/scenario@29dea3374ef4 snapshot 38fb07a586afa0be","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4b4c509d8490c6034ebe9f7b5219258734fa8275cfb3c59edcafbca0e263e091","slc_4fa4ac26db7aa0d91d147337f455aff166ae754ba4a68e85e7eba8b85aa8d334","slc_62c8f44e9da123185e555a8b27b1b47497d7fb8e08a5c112b28dcef8803f2bfb","slc_df40b0e8631d346573a063787f1214aecc87115ffc0096ce5d889a7aa57def9a"],"source_ids":["src_34db99264cff54e2817a13a0f63b1bcc"],"text":"Shipped agent components include a UserSimulatorAgent, a JudgeAgent evaluated against criteria, and a RedTeamAgent for multi-turn adversarial attacks such as Crescendo escalation with per-turn scoring and refusal detection.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_de79f4f9009aa18f84d25a0ea22c8d4c9ad5c82bc42070a08d8be4ad378be12b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"langwatch/scenario@29dea3374ef4 snapshot 38fb07a586afa0be","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1f5b6f6ad59a02716bff5a83b7cd8ccaf1d65d7b2c42ffaabf55512babbe4a3d","slc_c0c727a3a4ef54ed04f8167dbf663f8abbad7c78c53f806e71eba87ad768cfbf"],"source_ids":["src_34db99264cff54e2817a13a0f63b1bcc"],"text":"Scenario is described as an agent testing framework based on simulations, able to test real agent behavior by simulating users across scenarios and edge cases.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e504805d98f09534bb566fd3b02ad22a2b5ca49b769937560e4606978c0a5f9f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"langwatch/scenario@29dea3374ef4 snapshot 38fb07a586afa0be","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1e77cf0187e59639facdb0974ae4dd0d442a22b973b51b63aeff19c186db12ca","slc_e04e99280f3e771c8c6446cbb1074857fba86a00e0a44a953fc0b5052ae6876c","slc_f739029cc5a290fbfb3f1bc09f047e592c0b91b1157ba7df5a7ba0af49fea90c"],"source_ids":["src_34db99264cff54e2817a13a0f63b1bcc"],"text":"Debug mode shows messages step by step and allows human intervention mid-conversation; it is enabled via configure(debug=True), a per-scenario field, or the --scenario-debug pytest flag.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e5a3c19708be321cfb2b10e3c6bab24f61b70f189e7116de019ca46db314ecf5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"langwatch/scenario@29dea3374ef4 snapshot 38fb07a586afa0be","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1c53c3a2b8dc4f52ecf8fff9db70f227b7a23bfc95ee9a5b34955708db6691ba","slc_e319641b86d83473762d921455131fc42459abc6bbfc93d79ce6e76b9205fe85","slc_fc6c9556b822f2e50a6fbd765ca2c304e58db6011ab05af5e5e8c2f5d155da3e"],"source_ids":["src_642eefa88dda54e9bbf9b569a6ac8f63"],"text":"An accepted ADR replaces environment-variable configuration with per-call programmatic config: each run() gets its own EventBus, config and batchRunId, removing process-wide shared state and the need for a mutex.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:04:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fbc08600a3c48b09d668392fb1445ad"}
